{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-mechanism-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48 part E: `rates-mechanism`, the Rates-scale twin of `chain-so2-co2e-mechanism` -- the hydrocarbon chain, NonHAPTOG (88) with its mechanism (3000), the air toxics, SO2, N2O, atmospheric CO2, Total Energy and CO2 equivalent from running exhaust -- for the gasoline-selected passenger car in Washtenaw County on road types 1 and 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. The non-HAP TOG residual per speed bin: NMOG's finished rate minus the integrated species', clamped at zero per bin, because TOGSpeciationCalculator.sql's GROUP BY carries linkID, which is the bin at Rates scale. Beside it, the inventory's longest chains -- four rungs from THC, SO2 from energy in kilojoules, CO2AE's three parents by global warming potential -- each applied to the per-bin rate, and all of them for off-network idle.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate` = 13835, the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs across five road types, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-mechanism"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-mechanism/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
